<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We are interested in the problem of watermarking the output of large language models.
The token space is a finite set <math id="S1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=\{1,\ldots,d\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=\{1,\ldots,d\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> be the space of all finite sequences over alphabet <math id="S1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>.
A language model is a function <math id="S1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p:\Sigma^{*}\to\Delta(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p:\Sigma^{*}\to\Delta(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> is the space
of probability distributions over the tokens. Equivalently, <math id="S1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is a probability kernel from <math id="S1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>.
A sequence of tokens <math id="S1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1},\ldots,A_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1},\ldots,A_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is sampled autoregressively from <math id="S1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> in the usual way:</p>
<table id="S1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle A_{t}\sim p(\cdot|A_{1},\ldots,A_{t-1})=P_{t}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{t}\sim p(\cdot|A_{1},\ldots,A_{t-1})=P_{t}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Watermarking is a mechanism for sampling from the language model (preferably without distortion) in such a way that the owner
of the model can later distinguish those sequences that have been sampled from the model from those that have not.
The Gumbel watermarking scheme proposed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Aaronson (2022)</a></cite> works as follows (see <a href="#algorithm1" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>):</p>
<ol id="S1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <span id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">key</span> be a secret key known to the language model designer.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When sampling <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> from the model, use a hash function to produce a random seed
using <span id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">key</span> and <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t-1},\ldots,A_{t-k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t-1},\ldots,A_{t-k}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is some small integer. For example, <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=3</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Use this random seed to generate pseudorandom uniform variables <math id="S1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U_{t,a})_{a\in\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U_{t,a})_{a\in\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> and
then select</p>
<table id="S1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{t}=\operatornamewithlimits{arg\,max}_{a\in\Sigma}\frac{P_{t}(a)}{-\log(U_{t,a})}=\operatornamewithlimits{arg\,max}_{a\in\Sigma}\left[-\log(-\log(U_{t,a}))+\log(P_{t}(a))\right]\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{t}=\operatornamewithlimits{arg\,max}_{a\in\Sigma}\frac{P_{t}(a)}{-\log(U_{t,a})}=\operatornamewithlimits{arg\,max}_{a\in\Sigma}\left[-\log(-\log(U_{t,a}))+\log(P_{t}(a))\right]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Setting aside the issue that the <math id="S1.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U_{t,a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U_{t,a})</annotation></semantics></math> are only pseudorandom, the conditional law of <math id="S1.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S1.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> by the Gumbel trick and recalling that
<math id="S1.I1.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\log(-\log(U))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\log(-\log(U))</annotation></semantics></math> is Gumbel distributed when <math id="S1.I1.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly distributed on <math id="S1.I1.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="algorithm1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="36.41" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 482.22 36.41" width="482.22"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,36.41) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(241.11,0) translate(0,12.69)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E6E6E6;" fill="#E6E6E6"><path d="M -240.83 -12.41 h 481.66 v 24.82 h -481.66 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -236.22 -3.84)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:34.14em;--ltx-fo-height:0.84em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="15.6" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.64)" width="472.4"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="algorithm1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:34.14em;">
<span id="algorithm1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"></span>
<span id="algorithm1.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_listing ltx_align_left ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><span class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></span>
<span id="lstnumberx1" class="ltx_listingline">
                        <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1</span>
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                      <span id="lstnumberx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">args</span><span id="lstnumberx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">:</span><span id="lstnumberx1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">key</span><span id="lstnumberx1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">,</span><span id="lstnumberx1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="lstnumberx1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">,</span><span id="lstnumberx1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">model</span><span id="lstnumberx1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx2" class="ltx_listingline">
                        <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2</span>
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                      <span id="lstnumberx2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">for</span><span id="lstnumberx2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="lstnumberx2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">to</span><span id="lstnumberx2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\infty</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="lstnumberx2.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">:</span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx3" class="ltx_listingline">
                        <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3</span>
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                      <span id="lstnumberx3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">  </span><span id="lstnumberx3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">let</span><span id="lstnumberx3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P_{t}=p(\cdot|A_{1},\ldots,A_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}=p(\cdot|A_{1},\ldots,A_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx4" class="ltx_listingline">
                        <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4</span>
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                      <span id="lstnumberx4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">  </span><span id="lstnumberx4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">let</span><span id="lstnumberx4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{t}=(\texttt{key},A_{t-1},A_{t-2},\ldots,A_{t-k})\in[0,1]^{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">key</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{t}=(\texttt{key},A_{t-1},A_{t-2},\ldots,A_{t-k})\in[0,1]^{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx5" class="ltx_listingline">
                        <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5</span>
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                      <span id="lstnumberx5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">  </span><span id="lstnumberx5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">output</span><span id="lstnumberx5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">token</span><span id="lstnumberx5.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}=\operatornamewithlimits{arg\,max}_{a\in\Sigma}P_{t}(a)/(-\log U_{t,a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}=\operatornamewithlimits{arg\,max}_{a\in\Sigma}P_{t}(a)/(-\log U_{t,a})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx6" class="ltx_listingline">
                        <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6</span>
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                      <span id="lstnumberx6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">  </span><span id="lstnumberx6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">if</span><span id="lstnumberx6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}=</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="lstnumberx6.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">:</span><span id="lstnumberx6.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx6.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">break</span>
</span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E6E617;" fill="#E6E617"><path d="M -70.38 1.93 h 140.75 v 21.52 h -140.75 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -65.76 9.23)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:9.53em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="131.91"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="algorithm1.pic1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">gumbel watermarking</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float">Algorithm 1: </span> The watermarking algorithm accepts a secret key and a model and autoregressively samples
a sequence of tokens until the  token is sampled.
The  function uses its input to compute a pseudorandom vector <math id="algorithm1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly distributed on <math id="algorithm1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Detection</h3>

<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Detection works by noting that, when given the secret key,
the sequence of noise random variables <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> can be reconstructed from the text <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then let <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{t}=U_{t,A_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{t}=U_{t,A_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
When the text is not watermarked one would expect <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{1},\ldots,V_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{1},\ldots,V_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> to behave like an i.i.d. sequence of random variables that are uniformly distributed on <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.
On the other hand, when the text is watermarked, then <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is not uniformly distributed unless <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is a Dirac.
Hence, the detector can identify the watermark by proving statistically that the observed <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(V_{t})_{t=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(V_{t})_{t=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> were not sampled i.i.d. from the uniform distribution.
Importantly, detection is possible without access to the model.
The generic detection mechanism is given in <a href="#algorithm2" title="In Detection ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="algorithm2.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="33.81" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 521.59 33.81" width="521.59"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,33.81) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(260.8,0) translate(0,12.06)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E6E6E6;" fill="#E6E6E6"><path d="M -260.52 -11.78 h 521.03 v 23.56 h -521.03 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -255.91 -3.21)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.99em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="14.34" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="511.84"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="algorithm2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:36.99em;">
<span id="algorithm2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"></span>
<span id="algorithm2.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_listing ltx_align_left ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><span class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></span>
<span id="lstnumberx7" class="ltx_listingline">
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1</span>
                          
                          
                          
                          
                          
                          
                          
                        <span id="lstnumberx7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">args</span><span id="lstnumberx7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">:</span><span id="lstnumberx7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">key</span><span id="lstnumberx7.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">,</span><span id="lstnumberx7.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="lstnumberx7.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">,</span><span id="lstnumberx7.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">confidence</span><span id="lstnumberx7.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">level</span><span id="lstnumberx7.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="lstnumberx7.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">and</span><span id="lstnumberx7.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.19" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1},\ldots,A_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1},\ldots,A_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx8" class="ltx_listingline">
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2</span>
                          
                          
                          
                          
                          
                          
                          
                        <span id="lstnumberx8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">set</span><span id="lstnumberx8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=\frac{\log(1/\delta)}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=\frac{\log(1/\delta)}{n}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="lstnumberx8.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">and</span><span id="lstnumberx8.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">compute</span><span id="lstnumberx8.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="lstnumberx8.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">so</span><span id="lstnumberx8.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">that</span><span id="lstnumberx8.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.16" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_serif ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></span><span id="lstnumberx8.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx8.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">holds</span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx9" class="ltx_listingline">
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3</span>
                          
                          
                          
                          
                          
                          
                          
                        <span id="lstnumberx9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">for</span><span id="lstnumberx9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="lstnumberx9.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx9.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">to</span><span id="lstnumberx9.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx9.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="lstnumberx9.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">:</span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx10" class="ltx_listingline">
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4</span>
                          
                          
                          
                          
                          
                          
                          
                        <span id="lstnumberx10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">  </span><span id="lstnumberx10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">let</span><span id="lstnumberx10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx10.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{t}=(\texttt{key},A_{t-1},A_{t-2},\ldots,A_{t-k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">key</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{t}=(\texttt{key},A_{t-1},A_{t-2},\ldots,A_{t-k})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx11" class="ltx_listingline">
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5</span>
                          
                          
                          
                          
                          
                          
                          
                        <span id="lstnumberx11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">  </span><span id="lstnumberx11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">let</span><span id="lstnumberx11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx11.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{t}=U_{t,A_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{t}=U_{t,A_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx12" class="ltx_listingline">
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6</span>
                          
                          
                          
                          
                          
                          
                          
                        <span id="lstnumberx12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">if</span><span id="lstnumberx12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="((V_{t})_{t=1}^{n},\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">((V_{t})_{t=1}^{n},\delta)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="lstnumberx12.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">:</span><span id="lstnumberx12.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">return</span><span id="lstnumberx12.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx12.9" class="ltx_text"></span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx13" class="ltx_listingline">
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7</span>
                          
                          
                          
                          
                          
                          
                          
                        <span id="lstnumberx13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">return</span><span id="lstnumberx13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx13.4" class="ltx_text"></span>
</span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E6E617;" fill="#E6E617"><path d="M -32.29 2.64 h 64.57 v 18.83 h -64.57 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -27.67 7.25)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="55.35"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="algorithm2.pic1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">detection</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float">Algorithm 2: </span> The detection algorithm accepts the secret key, the confidence level <math id="algorithm2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> that controls the
false positive rate and the sequence of tokens to be evaluated.
The  is a well-chosen statistical test that the <math id="algorithm2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(V_{t})_{t=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(V_{t})_{t=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent and uniformly distributed on <math id="algorithm2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>
at confidence level <math id="algorithm2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Various options are available as we discuss in <a href="#S2" title="2 Exponential detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#S3" title="3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Contribution</h3>

<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We study the Gumbel watermarking procedure (<a href="#algorithm1" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), but replace the detection test proposed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Aaronson (2022)</a></cite> with a new test that is theoretically more statistically efficient.
We prove nearly matching problem-dependent upper and lower bounds on the number of tokens needed to detect watermarked text.
Our bounds are in terms of an entropy-like quantity of the distribution of next-token distributions.
The lower bound applies to all watermarking schemes in the same framework (to be explained) and hence the Gumbel scheme combined with the new
detector is (in a certain sense) nearly optimal.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Related work</h3>

<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There are now a huge variety of schemes for watermarking language models, with a range of desiderata
and analysis objectives <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Piet et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.
A relatively recent summary of the current state-of-the-art can be found in the review by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ji et al. (2025)</a></cite>, but the field is growing incredibly rapidly.
Some schemes are distortionary in the sense that they change the distribution of the model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kirchenbauer et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2023</a>)</cite> while
others are non-distortionary <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Aaronson, 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dathathri et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.
Our work is based on the non-distortionary Gumbel watermarking scheme proposed and analysed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Aaronson (2022)</a></cite>.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Aaronson (2022)</a></cite> used a detection mechanism based on a different statistic than the one proposed here and proved that
detection occurs with high probability once <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=\Omega(\log(1/\delta)/\bar{H}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=\Omega(\log(1/\delta)/\bar{H}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{H}</annotation></semantics></math> the average entropy
(see <a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2 Exponential detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).
This is the detection time that seems to be obtained most naturally when the concentration analysis used is
not variance-aware <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Christ et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al. (2023)</a></cite> theoretically study watermarking procedures that are both distortion free and
distortionary. Perhaps the most relevant of their results is a proof that when <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}=p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}=p</annotation></semantics></math> is constant, then
detection is possible if <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=\Omega(\log(1/H(p))\log(1/\delta)/H(p))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=\Omega(\log(1/H(p))\log(1/\delta)/H(p))</annotation></semantics></math> and that this is optimal. But this result is not obtained
using a simple practical watermarking procedure.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tsur et al. (2025a)</a></cite> ambitiously tackle the problem of designing exactly optimal statistical watermarking/detection schemes
but focus principally on the single-shot case where only a single token is sampled from the model, with preliminary results
in the sequential setting with a constant token distribution (<math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}=p\,\forall t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}=p\,\forall t</annotation></semantics></math>).
Like us, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. (2025a)</a></cite> also examine the problem of refining the detection of Gumbel watermarking (and the scheme by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kuditipudi et al. (2023)</a></cite>). They propose a model-agnostic detector that is optimal in an asymptotic minimax framework where <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is assumed to
satisfy <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{a\in\Sigma}P_{t}(a)\leq 1-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{a\in\Sigma}P_{t}(a)\leq 1-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> for some user-provided constant <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
On the one hand, they are able to establish a kind of exact optimality. On the other hand, thanks to the minimax nature of their
optimality definition, it is unclear if their method achieves the same kind of near-optimal problem-dependent detection efficiency
as our proposal.
Our statistical test is inspired by the classical literature on goodness-of-fit tests, and particularly the Anderson–Darling test <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Anderson and Darling, 1952</a>)</cite>.
Goodness-of-fit tests have been used for Gumbel watermarking by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al. (2025)</a></cite>.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. (2025b)</a></cite> also use goodness-of-fit tests for detection. They primarily focus on a more complicated version of the problem where some of the text has been generated by an LLM
but other parts are human-generated. Nevertheless, they prove a kind of optimality in certain scenarios. At the same time, their results seem incomparable to ours.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notation</h3>

<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The sequence length <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and confidence level <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> are fixed throughout.
When <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> are probability measures on the same space and <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is absolutely continuous with respect to <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>, then
the relative entropy and <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-divergence between <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> are</p>
<table id="S1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{KL}(\mu,\nu)=\int\log\left(\frac{\operatorname{d}\!\mu}{\operatorname{d}\!\nu}(x)\right)\operatorname{d}\!\mu(x)\quad\text{and}\quad\chi^{2}(\mu,\nu)=\int\left(\frac{\operatorname{d}\!\mu}{\operatorname{d}\!\nu}(x)-1\right)^{2}\operatorname{d}\!\nu(x)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{KL}(\mu,\nu)=\int\log\left(\frac{\operatorname{d}\!\mu}{\operatorname{d}\!\nu}(x)\right)\operatorname{d}\!\mu(x)\quad\text{and}\quad\chi^{2}(\mu,\nu)=\int\left(\frac{\operatorname{d}\!\mu}{\operatorname{d}\!\nu}(x)-1\right)^{2}\operatorname{d}\!\nu(x)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The uniform probability measure on <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}([0,1])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}([0,1])</annotation></semantics></math>, which is also denoted by <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.
The <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra generated by <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U_{s})_{s=1}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U_{s})_{s=1}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A_{s})_{s=1}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{s})_{s=1}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{t}=\sigma(U_{1},A_{1},\ldots,U_{t},A_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{t}=\sigma(U_{1},A_{1},\ldots,U_{t},A_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Null and alternative hypotheses</h3>

<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our results on the correctness and detection time for the Gumbel watermarking scheme
depend on two probability measures. Under the null hypothesis <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> we assume that
<math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U_{t})_{t=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U_{t})_{t=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A_{t})_{t=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{t})_{t=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent
so that <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(V_{t})_{t=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(V_{t})_{t=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sequence of independent uniformly distributed random variables.
On the other hand, under the alternative hypothesis <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> we assume that
<math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U_{t})_{t=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U_{t})_{t=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sequence of independent random elements sampled from <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}([0,1]^{\Sigma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}([0,1]^{\Sigma})</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}=\operatornamewithlimits{arg\,max}_{a\in\Sigma}P_{t}(a)/(-\log(U_{t,a}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}=\operatornamewithlimits{arg\,max}_{a\in\Sigma}P_{t}(a)/(-\log(U_{t,a}))</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P_{t}=p(\cdot|A_{1},\ldots,A_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}=p(\cdot|A_{1},\ldots,A_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math>
is the next-token distribution generated by the model.
The expectation with respect to <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> is denoted by <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
These assumptions are not unusual for the analysis of watermarking schemes <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2025a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dathathri et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.
Care is needed, however, since the statistical assumptions are not strictly-speaking correct because
the <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U_{t})_{t=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U_{t})_{t=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are generated using pseudorandomness and with seeds constructed from the observed tokens.
The statistical assumption could in principle be justified using cryptographic arguments and with
certain modifications to the procedure for generating <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Empirical evidence suggests that
the distortion due to pseudorandomness does not impact model performance on downstream tasks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dathathri et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Entropy-like quantities</h3>

<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a distribution <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in\Delta(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in\Delta(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> let
<math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\epsilon}(a)=p(a)\bm{1}(p(a)\leq\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\epsilon}(a)=p(a)\bm{1}(p(a)\leq\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)=p(a)\bm{1}(p(a)&gt;\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)=p(a)\bm{1}(p(a)&gt;\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The entropy of a distribution <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in\Delta(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in\Delta(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined by
<math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H(p)=-\sum_{a\in\Sigma}p(a)\log p(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(p)=-\sum_{a\in\Sigma}p(a)\log p(a)</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\log 0=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\log 0=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
We also need another entropy-like quantity, defined for <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="S1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G^{q}(p)=\sum_{a\in\Sigma}\left(p(a)(1-p(a))\right)^{q}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G^{q}(p)=\sum_{a\in\Sigma}\left(p(a)(1-p(a))\right)^{q}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Lastly, define <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\epsilon}(p)=G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(p_{\epsilon})/\sqrt{\epsilon}+G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(p_{\epsilon}^{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\epsilon}(p)=G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(p_{\epsilon})/\sqrt{\epsilon}+G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(p_{\epsilon}^{c})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Exponential detection</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Gumbel scheme was proposed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Aaronson (2022)</a></cite>, who suggested the following simple detection mechanism.
Let <math id="S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}=\log(1/(1-V_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}=\log(1/(1-V_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under the null hypothesis <math id="S2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S_{t})_{t=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S_{t})_{t=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sequence of independent exponentially distributed random variables.
The detector can proclaim a sequence is watermarked if <math id="S2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is unusually large relative
to what would be expected under the null hypothesis.
In the language of <a href="#algorithm2" title="In Detection ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>,</p>
<table id="S2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left((V_{t})_{t=1}^{n},\delta\right)=\bm{1}\left(\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}\geq\tau_{\star}\right)\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left((V_{t})_{t=1}^{n},\delta\right)=\bm{1}\left(\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}\geq\tau_{\star}\right)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the critical threshold <math id="S2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen so that <math id="S2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{0}(\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}\geq\tau_{\star})=\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{0}(\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}\geq\tau_{\star})=\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Aaronson (2022)</a></cite> showed that under the alternative hypothesis <math id="S2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> has a larger mean than under the null and
that detection occurs with probability at least <math id="S2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=\Omega(\log(1/\delta)/\bar{H}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=\Omega(\log(1/\delta)/\bar{H}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> where</p>
<table id="S2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{H}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}H(P_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{H}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}H(P_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">is the average entropy.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Power law detection</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This paper is about an alternative detection method that is statistically more efficient, at least theoretically (<a href="#algorithm3" title="In 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).
The idea is to replace the exponential statistic in <a href="#S2" title="2 Exponential detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> with a truncated power law. The intuition for this choice is given in the discussion (<a href="#S6" title="6 Discussion ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).
Let <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> be a constant to be chosen later and</p>
<table id="S3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S(u)=\min\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon}},\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-u}}\right)-\mu\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S(u)=\min\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon}},\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-u}}\right)-\mu\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=2-\sqrt{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=2-\sqrt{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen so that <math id="S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[S(U)]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[S(U)]=0</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> has law <math id="S3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}([0,1])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}([0,1])</annotation></semantics></math>.
We will use the statistic <math id="S3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}=S(V_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}=S(V_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, which under the null hypothesis is a truncated power law.
By definition the optimal critical value <math id="S3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen so that</p>
<table id="S3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{0}\left(\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}\geq\tau_{\star}\right)=\delta\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{0}\left(\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}\geq\tau_{\star}\right)=\delta\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm3" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="algorithm3.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="45.03" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 521.59 45.03" width="521.59"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,45.03) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(260.8,0) translate(0,17)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E6E6E6;" fill="#E6E6E6"><path d="M -260.52 -16.72 h 521.03 v 33.44 h -521.03 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -255.91 1.73)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.99em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:1em;font-size:10pt;" height="24.22" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="511.84"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="algorithm3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:36.99em;">
<span id="algorithm3.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"></span>
<span id="algorithm3.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_listing ltx_align_left ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><span class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></span>
<span id="lstnumberx14" class="ltx_listingline">
                        <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1</span>
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                      <span id="lstnumberx14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">args</span><span id="lstnumberx14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">:</span><span id="lstnumberx14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx14.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">key</span><span id="lstnumberx14.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">,</span><span id="lstnumberx14.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx14.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="lstnumberx14.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">,</span><span id="lstnumberx14.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx14.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">confidence</span><span id="lstnumberx14.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx14.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">level</span><span id="lstnumberx14.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx14.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="lstnumberx14.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx14.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">and</span><span id="lstnumberx14.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx14.19" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1},\ldots,A_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1},\ldots,A_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx15" class="ltx_listingline">
                        <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2</span>
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                      <span id="lstnumberx15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">set</span><span id="lstnumberx15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=\frac{\log(1/\delta)}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=\frac{\log(1/\delta)}{n}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="lstnumberx15.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">and</span><span id="lstnumberx15.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">compute</span><span id="lstnumberx15.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="lstnumberx15.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">so</span><span id="lstnumberx15.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">that</span><span id="lstnumberx15.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.16" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_serif ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></span><span id="lstnumberx15.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">holds</span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx16" class="ltx_listingline">
                        <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3</span>
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                      <span id="lstnumberx16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">for</span><span id="lstnumberx16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx16.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="lstnumberx16.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx16.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">to</span><span id="lstnumberx16.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx16.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="lstnumberx16.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">:</span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx17" class="ltx_listingline">
                        <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4</span>
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                      <span id="lstnumberx17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">  </span><span id="lstnumberx17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">let</span><span id="lstnumberx17.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx17.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{t}=(\texttt{key},A_{t-1},A_{t-2},\ldots,A_{t-k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">key</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{t}=(\texttt{key},A_{t-1},A_{t-2},\ldots,A_{t-k})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx18" class="ltx_listingline">
                        <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5</span>
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                      <span id="lstnumberx18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">  </span><span id="lstnumberx18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">let</span><span id="lstnumberx18.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx18.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{t}=U_{t,A_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{t}=U_{t,A_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="lstnumberx18.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx18.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">and</span><span id="lstnumberx18.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx18.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}=S(V_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}=S(V_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx19" class="ltx_listingline">
                        <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6</span>
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                      <span id="lstnumberx19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">if</span><span id="lstnumberx19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx19.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"><math id="lstnumberx19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}\geq\tau_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}\geq\tau_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="lstnumberx19.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">:</span><span id="lstnumberx19.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx19.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">return</span><span id="lstnumberx19.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx19.9" class="ltx_text"></span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx20" class="ltx_listingline">
                        <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7</span>
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                      <span id="lstnumberx20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">return</span><span id="lstnumberx20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx20.4" class="ltx_text"></span>
</span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E6E617;" fill="#E6E617"><path d="M -64.98 6.23 h 129.95 v 21.52 h -129.95 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -60.36 13.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.78em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="121.5"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="algorithm3.pic1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">power law detection</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float">Algorithm 3: </span> The power law detection algorithm accepts the secret key, the confidence level <math id="algorithm3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> that controls the
false positive rate and the sequence of tokens to be evaluated.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The definition of <math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> ensures the false positive rate is exactly <math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Naturally you can use a conservatively large
choice of <math id="S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> and still guarantee the false positive rate is at most <math id="S3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Such a choice is given in <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ Step 2: Case-by-case argument ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under the null hypothesis <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> has the same distribution as <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(U)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> has law <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}([0,1])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}([0,1])</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> can be estimated to high precision using Monte Carlo.
But note that <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> depends on the number of tokens <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> as well as the confidence level <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and the choice of <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>
that defines <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Let us note in passing that the requirement to know <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> can be relaxed by using anytime tests, a program that was recently
initiated for watermarking by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al. (2026)</a></cite>.
The exact asymptotics of <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> are discussed in <a href="#S6" title="6 Discussion ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">What remains is to understand the circumstances under which detection algorithm successfully identifies
watermarked text.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <a href="#algorithm3" title="In 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> is run with input <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A_{t})_{t=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{t})_{t=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> sampled using <a href="#algorithm1" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and using the same key
and <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=\log(1/\delta)/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=\log(1/\delta)/n</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{1}\left(\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})\geq C\tau\text{ and \lx@cref{creftype~refnum}{alg:detect} returns }\right)\leq 2\delta\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> and </mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#algorithm3" title="In 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> returns </mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{1}\left(\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})\geq C\tau\text{ and \lx@cref{creftype~refnum}{alg:detect} returns }\right)\leq 2\delta\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a universal constant and <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\Theta\big(\sqrt{n\log(n)\log(1/\delta)}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\Theta\big(\sqrt{n\log(n)\log(1/\delta)}\big)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ Step 2: Case-by-case argument ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In order to prove <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>
we need to analyse the distribution of the test statistic <math id="S3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> under the alternative hypothesis <math id="S3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular,
we will show that with high probability it scales proportionally to <math id="S3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Beyond this, we also need to argue that <math id="S3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is not too large.
To begin the analysis, we study the (conditional) law of <math id="S3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> under
both the null and alternative hypotheses.
For completeness, a proof of the following lemma is provided in the appendix.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fernandez et al. 2023</a></cite>)<span id="Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in\Delta(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in\Delta(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U_{a})_{a\in\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U_{a})_{a\in\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent standard uniform distributions and</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A=\operatornamewithlimits{arg\,max}_{a\in\Sigma}\frac{p(a)}{-\log(U_{a})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A=\operatornamewithlimits{arg\,max}_{a\in\Sigma}\frac{p(a)}{-\log(U_{a})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=U_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=U_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(V\leq x)=\sum_{a\in\Sigma}p(a)x^{1/p(a)}\leq x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(V\leq x)=\sum_{a\in\Sigma}p(a)x^{1/p(a)}\leq x</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that by definition if <math id="S3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> has law <math id="S3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}([0,1])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}([0,1])</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[S(U)]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[S(U)]=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
The next lemma provides a lower bound on <math id="S3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[S(V)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[S(V)]</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as in <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3 ( ). ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the same assumptions as <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3 ( ). ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and provided <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\leq 1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\leq 1/4</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[S(V)\right]\geq c\left[G_{\epsilon}(p)-\sqrt{\epsilon}\right]\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[S(V)\right]\geq c\left[G_{\epsilon}(p)-\sqrt{\epsilon}\right]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is an absolute constant and can be taken to be <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=\frac{1}{240}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>240</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=\frac{1}{240}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We proceed in two steps.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 1: Setup and main argument</h3>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=2-\sqrt{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=2-\sqrt{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By <a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3 ( ). ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>,</p>
<table id="S3.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[S(V)]=\int_{0}^{1}\sum_{a\in\Sigma}x^{1/p(a)-1}\min\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-x}},\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon}}\right)\operatorname{d}\!x-\mu=\sum_{a\in\Sigma}\delta_{\epsilon}(p(a))\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[S(V)]=\int_{0}^{1}\sum_{a\in\Sigma}x^{1/p(a)-1}\min\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-x}},\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon}}\right)\operatorname{d}\!x-\mu=\sum_{a\in\Sigma}\delta_{\epsilon}(p(a))\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where for <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S3.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\delta_{\epsilon}(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta_{\epsilon}(q)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\triangleq\int_{0}^{1}x^{1/q-1}\min\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-x}},\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon}}\right)\operatorname{d}\!x-q\mu\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\triangleq\int_{0}^{1}x^{1/q-1}\min\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-x}},\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon}}\right)\operatorname{d}\!x-q\mu\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">A case-by-case analysis shows that if <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in(0,1/4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in(0,1/4)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="S3.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\delta_{\epsilon}(q)\geq\frac{1}{120}\min\left(\sqrt{q},q/\sqrt{\epsilon}\right)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>120</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta_{\epsilon}(q)\geq\frac{1}{120}\min\left(\sqrt{q},q/\sqrt{\epsilon}\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Suppose that <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(a)&gt;1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(a)&gt;1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="S3.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{p(a)(1-p(a))}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{p(a)(1-p(a))}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sqrt{1-p(a)}=\sqrt{\sum_{b\neq a}p(b)}\leq\sum_{b\neq a}\min\left(\sqrt{p(b)},\frac{p(b)}{\sqrt{\epsilon}}\right)+\frac{\sqrt{\epsilon}}{4}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sqrt{1-p(a)}=\sqrt{\sum_{b\neq a}p(b)}\leq\sum_{b\neq a}\min\left(\sqrt{p(b)},\frac{p(b)}{\sqrt{\epsilon}}\right)+\frac{\sqrt{\epsilon}}{4}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where the final inequality follows using the fact that for <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{x+y}\leq\sqrt{x}+\sqrt{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>y</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{x+y}\leq\sqrt{x}+\sqrt{y}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{x}\leq x/(2y)+y/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{x}\leq x/(2y)+y/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=\{a:p(a)&gt;1/2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=\{a:p(a)&gt;1/2\}</annotation></semantics></math>, which of course has <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|M|\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|M|\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence</p>
<table id="S3.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G_{\epsilon}(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G_{\epsilon}(p)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{a\in M}\sqrt{p(a)(1-p(a))}+\sum_{b\in M^{c}}\min(\sqrt{p(b)},p(b)/\sqrt{\epsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msqrt><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{a\in M}\sqrt{p(a)(1-p(a))}+\sum_{b\in M^{c}}\min(\sqrt{p(b)},p(b)/\sqrt{\epsilon})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\sum_{b\in M^{c}}\min(\sqrt{p(b)},p(b)/\sqrt{\epsilon})+\frac{\sqrt{\epsilon}}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\sum_{b\in M^{c}}\min(\sqrt{p(b)},p(b)/\sqrt{\epsilon})+\frac{\sqrt{\epsilon}}{4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">by <a href="#S3.E6" title="In Step 1: Setup and main argument ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a></span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 240\sum_{b\in M^{c}}\delta_{\epsilon}(p(b))+\frac{\sqrt{\epsilon}}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>240</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 240\sum_{b\in M^{c}}\delta_{\epsilon}(p(b))+\frac{\sqrt{\epsilon}}{4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">by <a href="#S3.E5" title="In Step 1: Setup and main argument ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 240\mathbb{E}[S(V)]+\frac{\sqrt{\epsilon}}{4}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>240</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 240\mathbb{E}[S(V)]+\frac{\sqrt{\epsilon}}{4}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">by <a href="#S3.E4" title="In Step 1: Setup and main argument ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Rearranging completes the proof.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 2: Case-by-case argument</h3>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We finish the proof by confirming <a href="#S3.E5" title="In Step 1: Setup and main argument ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.
The function <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\mapsto\delta_{\epsilon}(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\mapsto\delta_{\epsilon}(q)</annotation></semantics></math> is concave and <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\epsilon}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\epsilon}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and for <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in(0,1/4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in(0,1/4)</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\epsilon}(1/2)\geq 1/10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\epsilon}(1/2)\geq 1/10</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\epsilon}(q)\geq 2q\delta_{\epsilon}(1/2)\geq q/5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\epsilon}(q)\geq 2q\delta_{\epsilon}(1/2)\geq q/5</annotation></semantics></math>.
<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geq 1/192" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>192</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geq 1/192</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\epsilon}(q)\geq q/5\geq\frac{1}{70}\sqrt{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>70</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\epsilon}(q)\geq q/5\geq\frac{1}{70}\sqrt{q}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, if
<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\epsilon}\geq 1/24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\epsilon}\geq 1/24</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\epsilon}(q)\geq q/5\geq\frac{1}{120}q/\sqrt{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>120</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\epsilon}(q)\geq q/5\geq\frac{1}{120}q/\sqrt{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Suppose now that <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q&lt;1/192" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>192</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q&lt;1/192</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\epsilon}&lt;1/24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\epsilon}&lt;1/24</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> be such that <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{1/q-1}=1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{1/q-1}=1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, which satisfies <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=(1/2)^{q/(1-q)}=\exp(-\frac{q}{1-q}\log(2))\leq 1-\frac{q\log(2)}{2(1-q)}\leq 1-q/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=(1/2)^{q/(1-q)}=\exp(-\frac{q}{1-q}\log(2))\leq 1-\frac{q\log(2)}{2(1-q)}\leq 1-q/3</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then</p>
<table id="S3.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\delta_{\epsilon}(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta_{\epsilon}(q)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1-\epsilon}\frac{x^{1/q-1}-q}{\sqrt{1-x}}+\sqrt{\frac{1}{\epsilon}}\int_{1-\epsilon}^{1}(x^{1/q-1}-q)\operatorname{d}\!x=\int_{0}^{1}x^{1/q-1}\min\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-x}},\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon}}\right)+q\left(\sqrt{\epsilon}-2\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1-\epsilon}\frac{x^{1/q-1}-q}{\sqrt{1-x}}+\sqrt{\frac{1}{\epsilon}}\int_{1-\epsilon}^{1}(x^{1/q-1}-q)\operatorname{d}\!x=\int_{0}^{1}x^{1/q-1}\min\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-x}},\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon}}\right)+q\left(\sqrt{\epsilon}-2\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(a)}}}}}{{\geq}}\frac{1}{2}\min\left(\sqrt{1-y},\frac{1-y}{\sqrt{\epsilon}}\right)-2q\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(b)}}}}}{{\geq}}\frac{1}{2}\min\left(\sqrt{q/3},\frac{q}{3\sqrt{\epsilon}}\right)-2q\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(c)}}}}}{{\geq}}\frac{1}{4}\min\left(\sqrt{q/3},\frac{q}{3\sqrt{\epsilon}}\right)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≥</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(a)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mover><mo>≥</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(b)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mover><mo>≥</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(c)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(a)}}}}}{{\geq}}\frac{1}{2}\min\left(\sqrt{1-y},\frac{1-y}{\sqrt{\epsilon}}\right)-2q\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(b)}}}}}{{\geq}}\frac{1}{2}\min\left(\sqrt{q/3},\frac{q}{3\sqrt{\epsilon}}\right)-2q\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(c)}}}}}{{\geq}}\frac{1}{4}\min\left(\sqrt{q/3},\frac{q}{3\sqrt{\epsilon}}\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(a)</span> follows since the integrand is increasing, <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(b)</span> since <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\leq 1-q/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\leq 1-q/3</annotation></semantics></math> and <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(c)</span> since <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q&lt;1/192" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>192</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q&lt;1/192</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\epsilon}&lt;1/24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\epsilon}&lt;1/24</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The critical value <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in <a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> can be upper bounded using a concentration of measure argument.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> for some <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tau_{\star}\leq\sqrt{-2n\log(\epsilon)\log(1/\delta)}+\frac{3\log(1/\delta)}{2\sqrt{\epsilon}}\triangleq\tau\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tau_{\star}\leq\sqrt{-2n\log(\epsilon)\log(1/\delta)}+\frac{3\log(1/\delta)}{2\sqrt{\epsilon}}\triangleq\tau\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Under the null hypothesis <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(V_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(V_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is a sequence of independent uniform random variables.
By definition, <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}=S(V_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}=S(V_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and hence <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|S_{t}|\leq 1/\sqrt{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|S_{t}|\leq 1/\sqrt{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, an elementary integral shows that <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{0}[S_{t}^{2}]\leq-\log\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{0}[S_{t}^{2}]\leq-\log\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, by Bernstein’s inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Boucheron et al., 2013</a>)</cite>, with <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>-probability at least <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sqrt{-2n\log(\epsilon)\log(1/\delta)}+\frac{3\log(1/\delta)}{2\sqrt{\epsilon}}=\tau\,.\qed" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sqrt{-2n\log(\epsilon)\log(1/\delta)}+\frac{3\log(1/\delta)}{2\sqrt{\epsilon}}=\tau\,.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ Step 2: Case-by-case argument ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> shows that under the null hypothesis the statistics are upper bounded with high probability.
The next lemma shows that under the alternative hypothesis they can be lower bounded with high probability.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=\log(1/\delta)/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=\log(1/\delta)/n</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, with <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-probability at least <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-2\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-2\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}\geq\frac{c}{2}\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})-3\tau\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}\geq\frac{c}{2}\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})-3\tau\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> is the constant in <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ Step 2: Case-by-case argument ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{t}(x)=\mathbb{P}_{1}(V_{t}\leq x|\mathcal{F}_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{t}(x)=\mathbb{P}_{1}(V_{t}\leq x|\mathcal{F}_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{t}=F_{t}(V_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{t}=F_{t}(V_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, which under
<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{1}(\cdot|\mathcal{F}_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{1}(\cdot|\mathcal{F}_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly distributed.
By <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3 ( ). ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{t}\leq V_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{t}\leq V_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, which means that</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{t}\triangleq\min\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon}},\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-W_{t}}}\right)-\mu\leq\min\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon}},\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-V_{t}}}\right)-\mu\triangleq S_{t}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>≜</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{t}\triangleq\min\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon}},\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-W_{t}}}\right)-\mu\leq\min\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon}},\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-V_{t}}}\right)-\mu\triangleq S_{t}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}-R_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}-R_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-negative and <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}-R_{t}\leq 1/\sqrt{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}-R_{t}\leq 1/\sqrt{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, by <a href="#Thmtheorem23" title="Lemma 23 ( ). ‣ Appendix A Technical inequalities ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>, with <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-probability at least <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{n}(S_{t}-R_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{n}(S_{t}-R_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(a)}}}}}{{\geq}}\sum_{t=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{1}[S_{t}-R_{t}|\mathcal{F}_{t-1}]-\sqrt{\epsilon}\sum_{t=1}^{n}\frac{\mathbb{E}_{1}\left[(S_{t}-R_{t})^{2}|\mathcal{F}_{t-1}\right]}{2}-\frac{2\log(1/\delta)}{\sqrt{\epsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≥</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(a)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(a)}}}}}{{\geq}}\sum_{t=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{1}[S_{t}-R_{t}|\mathcal{F}_{t-1}]-\sqrt{\epsilon}\sum_{t=1}^{n}\frac{\mathbb{E}_{1}\left[(S_{t}-R_{t})^{2}|\mathcal{F}_{t-1}\right]}{2}-\frac{2\log(1/\delta)}{\sqrt{\epsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(b)}}}}}{{\geq}}\sum_{t=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{1}[S_{t}-R_{t}|\mathcal{F}_{t-1}]-\frac{1}{2}\sum_{t=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{1}\left[S_{t}-R_{t}|\mathcal{F}_{t-1}\right]-\frac{2\log(1/\delta)}{\sqrt{\epsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≥</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(b)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(b)}}}}}{{\geq}}\sum_{t=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{1}[S_{t}-R_{t}|\mathcal{F}_{t-1}]-\frac{1}{2}\sum_{t=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{1}\left[S_{t}-R_{t}|\mathcal{F}_{t-1}\right]-\frac{2\log(1/\delta)}{\sqrt{\epsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{t=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{1}[S_{t}-R_{t}|\mathcal{F}_{t-1}]-\frac{2\log(1/\delta)}{\sqrt{\epsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{t=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{1}[S_{t}-R_{t}|\mathcal{F}_{t-1}]-\frac{2\log(1/\delta)}{\sqrt{\epsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(c)}}}}}{{\geq}}\frac{c}{2}\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})-\frac{cn\sqrt{\epsilon}}{2}-\frac{2\log(1/\delta)}{\sqrt{\epsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≥</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(c)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(c)}}}}}{{\geq}}\frac{c}{2}\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})-\frac{cn\sqrt{\epsilon}}{2}-\frac{2\log(1/\delta)}{\sqrt{\epsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(d)}}}}}{{\geq}}\frac{c}{2}\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})-\frac{cn\sqrt{\epsilon}}{2}-\tau\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≥</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(d)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(d)}}}}}{{\geq}}\frac{c}{2}\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})-\frac{cn\sqrt{\epsilon}}{2}-\tau\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(a)</span> follows from <a href="#Thmtheorem23" title="Lemma 23 ( ). ‣ Appendix A Technical inequalities ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>,
<span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(b)</span> since <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}-R_{t}\in[0,1/\sqrt{\epsilon}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}-R_{t}\in[0,1/\sqrt{\epsilon}]</annotation></semantics></math>,
<span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(c)</span> from <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and
<span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(d)</span> from the definition of <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.
The law of <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the same as the law of <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, repeating the argument in <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ Step 2: Case-by-case argument ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> shows that
with <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-probability at least <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{n}R_{t}\geq-\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{n}R_{t}\geq-\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.
Combining the above with a union bound shows with probability at least <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-2\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-2\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t=1}^{n}(S_{t}-R_{t})+\sum_{t=1}^{n}R_{t}\geq\frac{c}{2}\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})-\frac{cn\sqrt{\epsilon}}{2}-2\tau\geq\frac{c}{2}\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})-3\tau\,.\qed" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t=1}^{n}(S_{t}-R_{t})+\sum_{t=1}^{n}R_{t}\geq\frac{c}{2}\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})-\frac{cn\sqrt{\epsilon}}{2}-2\tau\geq\frac{c}{2}\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})-3\tau\,.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=8/c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=8/c</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and
define events <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle E=\left\{\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})\geq C\tau\right\}\quad\text{and}\quad F=\left\{\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}\geq\frac{c}{2}\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})-3\tau\right\}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow><mtext>and</mtext><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>τ</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E=\left\{\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})\geq C\tau\right\}\quad\text{and}\quad F=\left\{\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}\geq\frac{c}{2}\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})-3\tau\right\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">By <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma 6. ‣ Step 2: Case-by-case argument ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(F)\geq 1-2\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(F)\geq 1-2\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Suppose that <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}&lt;\tau_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}&lt;\tau_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tau\geq\tau_{\star}&gt;\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}\geq\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}-\frac{c}{2}\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})+4\tau\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tau\geq\tau_{\star}&gt;\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}\geq\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}-\frac{c}{2}\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})+4\tau\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">which after arranging implies that <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{c}</annotation></semantics></math> holds.
Hence,</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\left(\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})\geq C\tau,\,\text{\lx@cref{creftype~refnum}{alg:detect} returns }\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mtext><a href="#algorithm3" title="In 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext><mtext> returns </mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\left(\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})\geq C\tau,\,\text{\lx@cref{creftype~refnum}{alg:detect} returns }\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}\left(E\text{ and }\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}&lt;\tau_{\star}\right)\leq\mathbb{P}\left(F^{c}\right)\leq 2\delta\,.\qed" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}\left(E\text{ and }\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}&lt;\tau_{\star}\right)\leq\mathbb{P}\left(F^{c}\right)\leq 2\delta\,.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> can be used to bound the detection time for
various synthetic representations of a language model.
By definition <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\Theta(\sqrt{n\log(n)\log(1/\delta)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\Theta(\sqrt{n\log(n)\log(1/\delta)})</annotation></semantics></math>, so detection is likely to occur whenever</p>
<table id="S3.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})=\Omega\left(\sqrt{n\log(n)\log(1/\delta)}\right)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})=\Omega\left(\sqrt{n\log(n)\log(1/\delta)}\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 7</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<span id="Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">no entropy</span>)<span id="Thmtheorem7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is a Dirac for all <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and detection does not occur with high probability.
Distortion-free watermarking is not possible without entropy.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 8</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<span id="Thmtheorem8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">constant low entropy</span>)<span id="Thmtheorem8.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}=p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}=p</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=(1-\beta,\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=(1-\beta,\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
<table id="S3.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G_{\epsilon}(p)=\Theta\left(\sqrt{\beta(1-\beta)}\right)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G_{\epsilon}(p)=\Theta\left(\sqrt{\beta(1-\beta)}\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem8.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Hence, by <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, detection occurs with probability at least <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-2\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-2\delta</annotation></semantics></math> if</p>
<table id="S3.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle nG_{\epsilon}(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle nG_{\epsilon}(p)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})=\Omega\left(\sqrt{n\log(n)\log(1/\delta)}\right)\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})=\Omega\left(\sqrt{n\log(n)\log(1/\delta)}\right)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem8.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which after substituting <a href="#S3.E8" title="In Example 8 (constant low entropy). ‣ Step 2: Case-by-case argument ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> is equivalent to
<math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=\Omega\left(\frac{\log(n)\log(1/\delta)}{\beta(1-\beta)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=\Omega\left(\frac{\log(n)\log(1/\delta)}{\beta(1-\beta)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 9</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<span id="Thmtheorem9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">rare high entropy</span>)<span id="Thmtheorem9.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is a Dirac with probability <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\beta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\beta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and otherwise <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}=p=(1/2,1/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}=p=(1/2,1/2)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\epsilon}(p)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\epsilon}(p)=1</annotation></semantics></math> and with high probability
<math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})=\Omega(\beta n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})=\Omega(\beta n)</annotation></semantics></math> and detection occurs once</p>
<table id="S3.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n=\Omega\left(\frac{\log(n)\log(1/\delta)}{\beta^{2}}\right)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n=\Omega\left(\frac{\log(n)\log(1/\delta)}{\beta^{2}}\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 10</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<span id="Thmtheorem10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">many rare tokens</span>)<span id="Thmtheorem10.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in(0,1/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in(0,1/2)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}=p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}=p</annotation></semantics></math> is constant with <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=(1-\beta,\beta/(d-1),\beta/(d-1),\ldots,\beta/(d-1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=(1-\beta,\beta/(d-1),\beta/(d-1),\ldots,\beta/(d-1))</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then</p>
<table id="S3.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G_{\epsilon}(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G_{\epsilon}(p)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\begin{cases}\sqrt{d\beta}&amp;\text{if }\beta/(d-1)\geq\epsilon\\
\sqrt{\beta}+\beta/\sqrt{\epsilon}&amp;\text{otherwise}\,.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msqrt></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msqrt><mi>β</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\begin{cases}\sqrt{d\beta}&amp;\text{if }\beta/(d-1)\geq\epsilon\\
\sqrt{\beta}+\beta/\sqrt{\epsilon}&amp;\text{otherwise}\,.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem10.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then detection occurs once <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=\Omega\left(\frac{\log(n)\log(1/\delta)}{\beta}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=\Omega\left(\frac{\log(n)\log(1/\delta)}{\beta}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that this is roughly the time it takes to see <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(\log(n)\log(1/\delta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(\log(n)\log(1/\delta))</annotation></semantics></math> rare tokens.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">The previous examples are specialisations of the general setting that <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P_{t})_{t=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P_{t})_{t=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is sampled from
a product measure <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 11</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<span id="Thmtheorem11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">iid setting</span>)<span id="Thmtheorem11.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P,P_{1},\ldots,P_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P,P_{1},\ldots,P_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent and identically distributed with law <math id="Thmtheorem11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})=O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})=O(1)</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely and that <math id="Thmtheorem11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{t})]\ll 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≪</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{t})]\ll 1</annotation></semantics></math> is small, which is
the interesting case.
By Hoeffding’s bound, with probability at least <math id="Thmtheorem11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S3.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq n\mathbb{E}[G_{\epsilon}(P)]-O\left(\sqrt{n\log(1/\delta)}\right)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq n\mathbb{E}[G_{\epsilon}(P)]-O\left(\sqrt{n\log(1/\delta)}\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem11.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Hence detection occurs with high probability once</p>
<table id="S3.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[G_{\epsilon}(P)]\approx\sqrt{\frac{\log(n)\log(1/\delta)}{n}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[G_{\epsilon}(P)]\approx\sqrt{\frac{\log(n)\log(1/\delta)}{n}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem11.p1.3" class="ltx_p">By definition,</p>
<table id="S3.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[G_{\epsilon}(P)\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(P_{\epsilon})/\sqrt{\epsilon}+G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{\epsilon}^{c})\right]\geq\max\left(\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(P_{\epsilon})]/\sqrt{\epsilon},\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{\epsilon}^{c})]\right)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[G_{\epsilon}(P)\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(P_{\epsilon})/\sqrt{\epsilon}+G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{\epsilon}^{c})\right]\geq\max\left(\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(P_{\epsilon})]/\sqrt{\epsilon},\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{\epsilon}^{c})]\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem11.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem11.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is the smallest value such that <a href="#S3.E9" title="In Example 11 (iid setting). ‣ Step 2: Case-by-case argument ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> holds.
By the definition of <math id="Thmtheorem11.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=\frac{\log(1/\delta)}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=\frac{\log(1/\delta)}{n}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S3.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n\approx\min\left(\frac{\sqrt{-\log(\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(P_{\epsilon})])}}{\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(P_{\epsilon})]},\,\frac{-\log(\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{\epsilon}^{c})])}{\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{\epsilon}^{c})]^{2}}\right)\log(1/\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n\approx\min\left(\frac{\sqrt{-\log(\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(P_{\epsilon})])}}{\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(P_{\epsilon})]},\,\frac{-\log(\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{\epsilon}^{c})])}{\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{\epsilon}^{c})]^{2}}\right)\log(1/\delta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem11.p1.5" class="ltx_p">This bound is not fully explicit, since <math id="Thmtheorem11.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> on the right-hand side depends on <math id="Thmtheorem11.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. Nevertheless, it serves as a useful comparison for our lower bound.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Lower bounds</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Gumbel watermarking procedure combined with the detection mechanism described above is nearly optimal in the setting where the detection process
cannot use the model.
We will formalise this by assuming that <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P_{t})_{t=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P_{t})_{t=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is an independent
and identically distributed sequence sampled from a suitably
symmetric distribution <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Before this, however, we provide a more-or-less known lower bound
that holds even if the model is known.
This result is essentially known already, though with a different proof <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al., 2023</a>)</cite>.
The bound holds for any sequential watermarking scheme, which we now formalise.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 12</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A sequential watermarking scheme is characterised by a probability kernel <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]\times\Delta(\Sigma)\to\Delta(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]\times\Delta(\Sigma)\to\Delta(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in\Delta(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in\Delta(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S4.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{1}\kappa(\cdot|u,p)\operatorname{d}\!u=p\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{1}\kappa(\cdot|u,p)\operatorname{d}\!u=p\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem12.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Kernels <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the above will be called valid selection kernels.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This definition is intended to be used with secret source of noise <math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U_{t})_{t=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U_{t})_{t=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> that is i.i.d. with law <math id="S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}([0,1])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}([0,1])</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 13</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem13.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Gumbel scheme can be recovered by letting <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\kappa(\cdot|u,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(\cdot|u,p)</annotation></semantics></math> be a Dirac on</p>
<table id="S4.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatornamewithlimits{arg\,max}_{a\in\Sigma}\frac{p(a)}{-\log\phi_{a}(u)}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatornamewithlimits{arg\,max}_{a\in\Sigma}\frac{p(a)}{-\log\phi_{a}(u)}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem13.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi_{a})_{a\in\Sigma}:[0,1]\to[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi_{a})_{a\in\Sigma}:[0,1]\to[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is a collection of functions such that <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi_{a}(U))_{a\in\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi_{a}(U))_{a\in\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> has law <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}([0,1]^{\Sigma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}([0,1]^{\Sigma})</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> has law <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}([0,1])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}([0,1])</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 14</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem14.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The kernel <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\kappa(\cdot|u,p)=p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(\cdot|u,p)=p</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to ignoring the source of randomness. That is, no watermarking.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem15" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 15</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem15.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem15.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U_{t})_{t=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U_{t})_{t=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is an i.i.d. sequence with law <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}([0,1])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}([0,1])</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> is a valid selection kernel (<a href="#Thmtheorem12" title="Definition 12. ‣ 4 Lower bounds ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>).
Under the null distribution <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> we assume that <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> has law <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(\cdot|A_{1},\ldots,A_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\cdot|A_{1},\ldots,A_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> and is independent of <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under the alternative distribution <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> it is assumed that <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is sampled from <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\kappa(\cdot|U_{t},P_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(\cdot|U_{t},P_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P_{t}=p(\cdot|A_{1},\ldots,A_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}=p(\cdot|A_{1},\ldots,A_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that <math id="S4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{t}=\sigma(A_{1},U_{1},\ldots,A_{t},U_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{t}=\sigma(A_{1},U_{1},\ldots,A_{t},U_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="S4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra generated by the information available to the detector.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem16" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 16</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem16.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem16.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem16.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> be the null and alternative measures defined in <a href="#Thmtheorem15" title="Assumption 15. ‣ 4 Lower bounds ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>.
Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-measurable and
<math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{0}(T=0)\geq 1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{0}(T=0)\geq 1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{1}(T=1)\geq 1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{1}(T=1)\geq 1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq\mathbb{E}[\bar{H}]^{-1}\log(1/(4\delta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq\mathbb{E}[\bar{H}]^{-1}\log(1/(4\delta))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{t}(X;Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{t}(X;Y)</annotation></semantics></math> be the mutual information between <math id="S4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="S4.p4.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{1}(\cdot|\mathcal{F}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{1}(\cdot|\mathcal{F}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the Bretagnolle–Huber inequality,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{P}_{0}(T=1)+\mathbb{P}_{1}(T=0)\geq\frac{1}{2}\exp\left(-\operatorname{KL}(\mathbb{P}_{1},\mathbb{P}_{0})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{P}_{0}(T=1)+\mathbb{P}_{1}(T=0)\geq\frac{1}{2}\exp\left(-\operatorname{KL}(\mathbb{P}_{1},\mathbb{P}_{0})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\exp\left(-\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{t=1}^{n}\operatorname{KL}(\mathbb{P}_{t-1}(U_{t},A_{t}\in\cdot),\mathbb{P}_{t-1}(U_{t}\in\cdot)\otimes\mathbb{P}_{t-1}(A_{t}\in\cdot))\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">∈</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">∈</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">∈</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\exp\left(-\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{t=1}^{n}\operatorname{KL}(\mathbb{P}_{t-1}(U_{t},A_{t}\in\cdot),\mathbb{P}_{t-1}(U_{t}\in\cdot)\otimes\mathbb{P}_{t-1}(A_{t}\in\cdot))\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\exp\left(-\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{t=1}^{n}I_{t-1}(U_{t};A_{t})\right]\right)\geq\frac{1}{2}\exp\left(-\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{t=1}^{n}H(P_{t})\right]\right)=\frac{1}{2}\exp\left(-n\mathbb{E}[\bar{H}]\right)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\exp\left(-\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{t=1}^{n}I_{t-1}(U_{t};A_{t})\right]\right)\geq\frac{1}{2}\exp\left(-\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{t=1}^{n}H(P_{t})\right]\right)=\frac{1}{2}\exp\left(-n\mathbb{E}[\bar{H}]\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Rearranging shows that <math id="S4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq\mathbb{E}[\bar{H}]^{-1}\log(1/(4\delta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq\mathbb{E}[\bar{H}]^{-1}\log(1/(4\delta))</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The Gumbel watermarking scheme combined with the new detection mechanism is nearly optimal when the model is not known and
when <math id="S4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> has law <math id="S4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for some distribution <math id="S4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The assumption that the model is not known is expressed by making a symmetry assumption on <math id="S4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem17" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 17</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem17.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A probability measure <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> is symmetric if when <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> has law <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\circ\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\circ\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> have the same law for any
permutation <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem18" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 18</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem18.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem18.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> is a symmetric probability measure on <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> is a valid selection kernel and <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\kappa_{0}(\cdot|u,p)=p(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{0}(\cdot|u,p)=p(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}_{0}=\lambda\otimes\xi\otimes\kappa_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}_{0}=\lambda\otimes\xi\otimes\kappa_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}_{1}=\lambda\otimes\xi\otimes\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}_{1}=\lambda\otimes\xi\otimes\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> be the law of <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1},A_{1},\ldots,U_{n},A_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1},A_{1},\ldots,U_{n},A_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U_{t},P_{t},A_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U_{t},P_{t},A_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> has law <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}_{k}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℚ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}_{k}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
That is <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is the law of <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U_{1},A_{1},\ldots,U_{n},A_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U_{1},A_{1},\ldots,U_{n},A_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> under the null hypothesis and <math id="Thmtheorem18.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the law of the same under the alternative hypothesis.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem19" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 19</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem19.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem19.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The symmetry assumption on <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> ensures that <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{1}(A_{t}\in\cdot)=\mathcal{U}(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">∈</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{1}(A_{t}\in\cdot)=\mathcal{U}(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence the marginals of both <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> are the same
under <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. But for <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> they are independent, which is not true for <math id="Thmtheorem19.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem20" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 20</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem20.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem20.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem20.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> are defined as in <a href="#Thmtheorem18" title="Assumption 18. ‣ 4 Lower bounds ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> and that
<math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-measurable and
<math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{0}(T=0)\geq 1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{0}(T=0)\geq 1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{1}(T=1)\geq 1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{1}(T=1)\geq 1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, for any <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in(0,1/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in(0,1/2)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> with law <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n\geq\min\left(\frac{1}{2\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(P_{\epsilon})]},\,\frac{\log\left(\frac{1}{16\delta}\right)}{16\mathbb{E}\left[G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{\epsilon}^{c})\right]^{2}}\right)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n\geq\min\left(\frac{1}{2\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(P_{\epsilon})]},\,\frac{\log\left(\frac{1}{16\delta}\right)}{16\mathbb{E}\left[G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{\epsilon}^{c})\right]^{2}}\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem20" title="Theorem 20. ‣ 4 Lower bounds ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We proceed in three steps.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 1: Setup and entropy inequalities</h3>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose that <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in(0,1/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in(0,1/2)</annotation></semantics></math> and <a href="#S4.E10" title="In Theorem 20. ‣ 4 Lower bounds ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> does not hold.
Then <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(P_{\epsilon})]&lt;\frac{1}{2n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(P_{\epsilon})]&lt;\frac{1}{2n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="E^{n}=\cap_{t=1}^{n}\{P_{t}(A_{t})&gt;\epsilon\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∩</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{n}=\cap_{t=1}^{n}\{P_{t}(A_{t})&gt;\epsilon\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that the law of <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the same under both <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> have law <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\sim P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\sim P</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</p>
<table id="S4.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{Q}^{n}_{0}(E^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{Q}^{n}_{0}(E^{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{Q}^{n}_{0}(P(A)&gt;\epsilon)^{n}=(1-\mathbb{Q}^{n}_{0}(P(A)\leq\epsilon))^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{Q}^{n}_{0}(P(A)&gt;\epsilon)^{n}=(1-\mathbb{Q}^{n}_{0}(P(A)\leq\epsilon))^{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(1-\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{a\in\Sigma}P(a)\bm{1}(P(a)\leq\epsilon)\right]\right)^{n}\geq\left(1-2\mathbb{E}\left[G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(P_{\epsilon})\right]\right)^{n}\geq\left(1-\frac{1}{n}\right)^{n}\geq\frac{1}{4}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(1-\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{a\in\Sigma}P(a)\bm{1}(P(a)\leq\epsilon)\right]\right)^{n}\geq\left(1-2\mathbb{E}\left[G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(P_{\epsilon})\right]\right)^{n}\geq\left(1-\frac{1}{n}\right)^{n}\geq\frac{1}{4}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the second inequality follows from the assumption that <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(P_{\epsilon})]&lt;1/(2n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(P_{\epsilon})]&lt;1/(2n)</annotation></semantics></math> and the first
from the fact that <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math> so that</p>
<table id="S4.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(P_{\epsilon})=\sum_{a:p(a)\leq\epsilon}p(a)(1-p(a))\geq\sum_{a:p(a)\leq\epsilon}p(a)/2\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(P_{\epsilon})=\sum_{a:p(a)\leq\epsilon}p(a)(1-p(a))\geq\sum_{a:p(a)\leq\epsilon}p(a)/2\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">From <a href="#S4.E11" title="In Step 1: Setup and entropy inequalities ‣ 4 Lower bounds ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> it follows that <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}^{n}_{0}(T=1|E^{n})=\mathbb{Q}^{n}_{0}(T=1,E^{n})/\mathbb{Q}_{0}(E^{n})\leq 4\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}^{n}_{0}(T=1|E^{n})=\mathbb{Q}^{n}_{0}(T=1,E^{n})/\mathbb{Q}_{0}(E^{n})\leq 4\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Similarly, <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}^{n}_{1}(T=0|E^{n})\leq 4\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}^{n}_{1}(T=0|E^{n})\leq 4\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, by the Bretagnolle–Huber inequality,</p>
<table id="S4.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 8\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 8\delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex42.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{Q}^{n}_{0}(T=1|E^{n})+\mathbb{Q}^{n}_{1}(T=0|E^{n})\geq\frac{1}{2}\exp\left(-\operatorname{KL}\right)\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{Q}^{n}_{0}(T=1|E^{n})+\mathbb{Q}^{n}_{1}(T=0|E^{n})\geq\frac{1}{2}\exp\left(-\operatorname{KL}\right)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\operatorname{KL}=\operatorname{KL}(\mathbb{Q}_{1}^{n}(U_{1},A_{1},\ldots,U_{n},A_{n}\in\cdot|E^{n}),\mathbb{Q}_{0}^{n}(U_{1},A_{1},\ldots,U_{n},A_{n}\in\cdot|E^{n}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">∈</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">∈</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{KL}=\operatorname{KL}(\mathbb{Q}_{1}^{n}(U_{1},A_{1},\ldots,U_{n},A_{n}\in\cdot|E^{n}),\mathbb{Q}_{0}^{n}(U_{1},A_{1},\ldots,U_{n},A_{n}\in\cdot|E^{n}))</annotation></semantics></math>.
Now <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{Q}^{n}_{k}(\cdot|E^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℚ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}^{n}_{k}(\cdot|E^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> is a product measure for both <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, abbreviating <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=U_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=U_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=\mathcal{U}([0,1])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=\mathcal{U}([0,1])</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m21" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="E=\{P(A)&gt;\epsilon\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=\{P(A)&gt;\epsilon\}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S4.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{KL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>KL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{KL}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex43.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=n\operatorname{KL}(\mathbb{Q}_{1}(U,A\in\cdot|E),\mathbb{Q}_{0}(U,A\in\cdot|E))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0em">∈</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0em">∈</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=n\operatorname{KL}(\mathbb{Q}_{1}(U,A\in\cdot|E),\mathbb{Q}_{0}(U,A\in\cdot|E))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=n\sum_{a\in\Sigma}\mathbb{Q}_{1}(A=a|E)\operatorname{KL}(\mathbb{Q}_{1}(U\in\cdot|A=a,E),\mathbb{Q}_{0}(U\in\cdot|A=a,E))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>E</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo rspace="0em">∈</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo rspace="0em">∈</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=n\sum_{a\in\Sigma}\mathbb{Q}_{1}(A=a|E)\operatorname{KL}(\mathbb{Q}_{1}(U\in\cdot|A=a,E),\mathbb{Q}_{0}(U\in\cdot|A=a,E))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=n\sum_{a\in\Sigma}\mathbb{Q}_{1}(A=a|E)\operatorname{KL}(\mathbb{Q}_{1}(U\in\cdot|A=a,E),\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>E</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo rspace="0em">∈</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=n\sum_{a\in\Sigma}\mathbb{Q}_{1}(A=a|E)\operatorname{KL}(\mathbb{Q}_{1}(U\in\cdot|A=a,E),\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{n}{d}\sum_{a\in\Sigma}\chi^{2}(\mathbb{Q}_{1}(U\in\cdot|A=a,E),\lambda)\,,\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo rspace="0em">∈</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{n}{d}\sum_{a\in\Sigma}\chi^{2}(\mathbb{Q}_{1}(U\in\cdot|A=a,E),\lambda)\,,\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where the inequality follows from <a href="#Thmtheorem22" title="Lemma 22 ( ). ‣ Appendix A Technical inequalities ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a> and because <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}_{1}(A=a|E)=1/d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}_{1}(A=a|E)=1/d</annotation></semantics></math> by the symmetry assumption.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 2: Bounding the chi-squared divergence</h3>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We start by introducing a variety of conditional measures (regular versions):</p>
<ul id="S4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\xi(\cdot|a)=\mathbb{Q}_{1}(P=\cdot|A=a,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi(\cdot|a)=\mathbb{Q}_{1}(P=\cdot|A=a,E)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu(\cdot|a)=\mathbb{Q}_{1}(U=\cdot|A=a,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\cdot|a)=\mathbb{Q}_{1}(U=\cdot|A=a,E)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu(\cdot|a,p)=\mathbb{Q}_{1}(U=\cdot|P,A=a,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\cdot|a,p)=\mathbb{Q}_{1}(U=\cdot|P,A=a,E)</annotation></semantics></math> evaluated at <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">By Bayes’ law, when <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(a)&gt;\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(a)&gt;\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="S4.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\operatorname{d}\!\xi(\cdot|a)}{\operatorname{d}\!\xi}(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\operatorname{d}\!\xi(\cdot|a)}{\operatorname{d}\!\xi}(p)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{dp_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)}{\mathbb{Q}_{1}(E)}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{dp_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)}{\mathbb{Q}_{1}(E)}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Next, if <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(a)&gt;\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(a)&gt;\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="S4.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\operatorname{d}\!\mu(\cdot|a,p)}{\operatorname{d}\!\lambda}(x)=\frac{\kappa(a|x,p)}{\int_{0}^{1}\kappa(a|y,p)\operatorname{d}\!y}\leq\frac{1}{p_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\operatorname{d}\!\mu(\cdot|a,p)}{\operatorname{d}\!\lambda}(x)=\frac{\kappa(a|x,p)}{\int_{0}^{1}\kappa(a|y,p)\operatorname{d}\!y}\leq\frac{1}{p_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> be independent of <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and have law <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\chi^{2}(\mu(\cdot|a),\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\chi^{2}(\mu(\cdot|a),\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\left(\frac{\operatorname{d}\!\mu(\cdot|a)}{\operatorname{d}\!\lambda}(x)-1\right)^{2}\operatorname{d}\!x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\left(\frac{\operatorname{d}\!\mu(\cdot|a)}{\operatorname{d}\!\lambda}(x)-1\right)^{2}\operatorname{d}\!x</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\operatorname{d}\!\mu(\cdot|a)}{\operatorname{d}\!\lambda}(x)^{2}\operatorname{d}\!x-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\operatorname{d}\!\mu(\cdot|a)}{\operatorname{d}\!\lambda}(x)^{2}\operatorname{d}\!x-1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(a)}}}}}{{=}}\int_{0}^{1}\left(\int_{\Delta(\Sigma)}\frac{\operatorname{d}\!\mu(\cdot|a,p)}{\operatorname{d}\!\lambda}(x)\operatorname{d}\!\xi(p|a)\right)^{2}\operatorname{d}\!x-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(a)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(a)}}}}}{{=}}\int_{0}^{1}\left(\int_{\Delta(\Sigma)}\frac{\operatorname{d}\!\mu(\cdot|a,p)}{\operatorname{d}\!\lambda}(x)\operatorname{d}\!\xi(p|a)\right)^{2}\operatorname{d}\!x-1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\Delta(\Sigma)}\int_{\Delta(\Sigma)}\left[\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\operatorname{d}\!\mu(\cdot|a,p)}{\operatorname{d}\!\lambda}(x)\frac{\operatorname{d}\!\mu(\cdot|a,q)}{\operatorname{d}\!\lambda}(x)\operatorname{d}\!x\right]\operatorname{d}\!\xi(p|a)\operatorname{d}\!\xi(q|a)-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\Delta(\Sigma)}\int_{\Delta(\Sigma)}\left[\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\operatorname{d}\!\mu(\cdot|a,p)}{\operatorname{d}\!\lambda}(x)\frac{\operatorname{d}\!\mu(\cdot|a,q)}{\operatorname{d}\!\lambda}(x)\operatorname{d}\!x\right]\operatorname{d}\!\xi(p|a)\operatorname{d}\!\xi(q|a)-1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(b)}}}}}{{\leq}}\int_{\Delta(\Sigma)}\int_{\Delta(\Sigma)}\min\left(\frac{1}{p_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)},\frac{1}{q_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)}\right)\operatorname{d}\!\xi(p|a)\operatorname{d}\!\xi(q|a)-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(b)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(b)}}}}}{{\leq}}\int_{\Delta(\Sigma)}\int_{\Delta(\Sigma)}\min\left(\frac{1}{p_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)},\frac{1}{q_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)}\right)\operatorname{d}\!\xi(p|a)\operatorname{d}\!\xi(q|a)-1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\Delta(\Sigma)}\int_{\Delta(\Sigma)}\min\left(\frac{1-p_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)}{p_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)},\frac{1-q_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)}{q_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)}\right)\operatorname{d}\!\xi(p|a)\operatorname{d}\!\xi(q|a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\Delta(\Sigma)}\int_{\Delta(\Sigma)}\min\left(\frac{1-p_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)}{p_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)},\frac{1-q_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)}{q_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)}\right)\operatorname{d}\!\xi(p|a)\operatorname{d}\!\xi(q|a)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(c)}}}}}{{=}}\frac{d^{2}}{\mathbb{Q}_{1}(E)^{2}}\int_{\Delta(\Sigma)}\int_{\Delta(\Sigma)}\min\left(\frac{1-p_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)}{p_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)},\frac{1-q_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)}{q_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)}\right)p_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)q_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)\operatorname{d}\!\xi(p)\operatorname{d}\!\xi(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(c)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(c)}}}}}{{=}}\frac{d^{2}}{\mathbb{Q}_{1}(E)^{2}}\int_{\Delta(\Sigma)}\int_{\Delta(\Sigma)}\min\left(\frac{1-p_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)}{p_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)},\frac{1-q_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)}{q_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)}\right)p_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)q_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)\operatorname{d}\!\xi(p)\operatorname{d}\!\xi(q)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{d^{2}}{\mathbb{Q}_{1}(E)^{2}}\mathbb{E}\left[\min\left(Q_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)(1-P_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)),P_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)(1-Q_{\epsilon}^{c}(a))\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{d^{2}}{\mathbb{Q}_{1}(E)^{2}}\mathbb{E}\left[\min\left(Q_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)(1-P_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)),P_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)(1-Q_{\epsilon}^{c}(a))\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(d)}}}}}{{\leq}}16d^{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\min\left(P_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)(1-P_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)),\,Q_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)(1-Q_{\epsilon}^{c}(a))\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(d)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(d)}}}}}{{\leq}}16d^{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\min\left(P_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)(1-P_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)),\,Q_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)(1-Q_{\epsilon}^{c}(a))\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(e)}}}}}{{\leq}}16d^{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\sqrt{P_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)(1-P_{\epsilon}^{c}(a))}\right]^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mpadded style="width:0pt;" lspace="-3.9pt" width="0pt"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#990000" mathsize="0.710em">(e)</mtext></mpadded></mover><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathclap{\text{\tiny{\color[rgb]{0.6,0,0}(e)}}}}}{{\leq}}16d^{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\sqrt{P_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)(1-P_{\epsilon}^{c}(a))}\right]^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where <span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(a)</span> follows from the definition of <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu(\cdot|a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\cdot|a)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu(\cdot|a,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\cdot|a,p)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi(p|a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi(p|a)</annotation></semantics></math>,
<span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(b)</span> from <a href="#S4.E14" title="In Step 2: Bounding the chi-squared divergence ‣ 4 Lower bounds ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>,
<span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(c)</span> from <a href="#S4.E13" title="In Step 2: Bounding the chi-squared divergence ‣ 4 Lower bounds ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>,
<span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(d)</span> since <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min(p(1-q),q(1-p))\leq\min(p(1-p),q(1-q))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min(p(1-q),q(1-p))\leq\min(p(1-p),q(1-q))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}_{0}(E)\geq\mathbb{Q}_{0}^{n}(E^{n})\geq 1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℚ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}_{0}(E)\geq\mathbb{Q}_{0}^{n}(E^{n})\geq 1/4</annotation></semantics></math> by <a href="#S4.E11" title="In Step 1: Setup and entropy inequalities ‣ 4 Lower bounds ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>. Finally,
<span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">(e)</span> holds because <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min(p(1-p),q(1-q))\leq\sqrt{p(1-p)q(1-q)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min(p(1-p),q(1-q))\leq\sqrt{p(1-p)q(1-q)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 3: Finishing up</h3>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Combining the result in the previous step with <a href="#S4.E12" title="In Step 1: Setup and entropy inequalities ‣ 4 Lower bounds ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>,</p>
<table id="S4.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{KL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>KL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{KL}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex56.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 16nd\sum_{a=1}^{d}\mathbb{E}\left[\sqrt{P_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)(1-P_{\epsilon}^{c}(a))}\right]^{2}=16n\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{a=1}^{d}\sqrt{P_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)(1-P_{\epsilon}^{c}(a))}\right]^{2}=16n\mathbb{E}\left[G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{\epsilon}^{c})\right]^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 16nd\sum_{a=1}^{d}\mathbb{E}\left[\sqrt{P_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)(1-P_{\epsilon}^{c}(a))}\right]^{2}=16n\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{a=1}^{d}\sqrt{P_{\epsilon}^{c}(a)(1-P_{\epsilon}^{c}(a))}\right]^{2}=16n\mathbb{E}\left[G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{\epsilon}^{c})\right]^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore
<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16\delta\geq\exp(-16n\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{\epsilon}^{c})]^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16\delta\geq\exp(-16n\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{\epsilon}^{c})]^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>,
which implies that</p>
<table id="S4.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n\geq\frac{\log\left(\frac{1}{16\delta}\right)}{16\mathbb{E}\left[G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{\epsilon}^{c})\right]^{2}}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n\geq\frac{\log\left(\frac{1}{16\delta}\right)}{16\mathbb{E}\left[G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{\epsilon}^{c})\right]^{2}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which contradicts our assumption that <a href="#S4.E10" title="In Theorem 20. ‣ 4 Lower bounds ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> does not hold.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Comparing upper and lower bounds</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The upper and lower bounds are nearly matching in the i.i.d. setting of <a href="#Thmtheorem11" title="Example 11 (iid setting). ‣ Step 2: Case-by-case argument ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Example</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>.
The upper bound shows that detection occurs with high probability with Gumbel watermarking and power law detection after observing <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq N_{\textsc{upper}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">upper</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq N_{\textsc{upper}}</annotation></semantics></math> tokens where
<math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\textsc{upper}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">upper</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\textsc{upper}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the smallest natural number such that</p>
<table id="S5.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle N_{\textsc{upper}}\approx\min\left(\frac{\sqrt{-\log\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(P_{\epsilon})]}}{\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(P_{\epsilon})]},\frac{-\log\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{\epsilon}^{c})]}{\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{\epsilon}^{c})]^{2}}\right)\log(1/\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">upper</mtext></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle N_{\textsc{upper}}\approx\min\left(\frac{\sqrt{-\log\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(P_{\epsilon})]}}{\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(P_{\epsilon})]},\frac{-\log\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{\epsilon}^{c})]}{\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{\epsilon}^{c})]^{2}}\right)\log(1/\delta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=\log(1/\delta)/N_{\textsc{upper}}\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">upper</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=\log(1/\delta)/N_{\textsc{upper}}\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math> with the inequality holding by the assumption in <a href="#Thmtheorem11" title="Example 11 (iid setting). ‣ Step 2: Case-by-case argument ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Example</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> that <math id="S5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P)]</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently small.
The lower bound (<a href="#Thmtheorem20" title="Theorem 20. ‣ 4 Lower bounds ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>) shows that detection cannot occur unless <math id="S5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq N_{\textsc{lower}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">lower</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq N_{\textsc{lower}}</annotation></semantics></math> where</p>
<table id="S5.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle N_{\textsc{lower}}\approx\min\left(\frac{1}{\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(P_{\epsilon})]},\,\frac{\log(1/\delta)}{\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{\epsilon}^{c})]^{2}}\right)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">lower</mtext></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle N_{\textsc{lower}}\approx\min\left(\frac{1}{\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$1$}}(P_{\epsilon})]},\,\frac{\log(1/\delta)}{\mathbb{E}[G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{\epsilon}^{c})]^{2}}\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Note that the lower bound holds for any <math id="S5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in(0,1/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in(0,1/2)</annotation></semantics></math>, and in particular for <math id="S5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=\log(1/\delta)/N_{\textsc{upper}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">upper</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=\log(1/\delta)/N_{\textsc{upper}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence the upper and lower bounds are separated by logarithmic factors.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Discussion</h2>

<section id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Experiments</h3>

<div id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">You surely noticed the absence of experiments.
Our brief tests showed the power law detector indeed outperforms the exponential detector in synthetically crafted examples where
the theory says it should (e.g., <a href="#Thmtheorem8" title="Example 8 (constant low entropy). ‣ Step 2: Case-by-case argument ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Example</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>).
Unfortunately, however, its performance on language data seems to be slightly worse, presumably due to the additional logarithmic factor and/or constant factors.
There may be ways to improve the proposed statistic to get the best of both worlds. Most naively one can combine both detectors with a union bound, but better methods
might be possible.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Detecting non-watermarked text</h3>

<div id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#algorithm3" title="In 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> either rejects the null hypothesis and returns  or returns
. The latter result does not correspond to a high-probability guarantee that the text is not
watermarked. Such an assertion is not possible in the standard frequentist setting considered here because the signal
provided by watermarking can be arbitrarily small when the entropy of the conditional distributions <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is small.
However, if there is a known (probabilistic) lower bound on <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{n}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, then it is possible
to accept the null hypothesis if <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> does not grow suitably fast.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Intuition for statistic</h3>

<div id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The intuition behind the definition of <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> is as follows.
The key statistical approach is based on testing whether or not <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(V_{t})_{t=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(V_{t})_{t=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> could reasonably be sampled from
a uniform distribution, which falls into the goodness-of-fit class of statistical tests <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">D’Agostino, 2017</a>)</cite>.
Many of these tests are based on some kind of comparison between the empirical CDF of <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(V_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(V_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and the CDF of the uniform
distribution, which for <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(x)=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(x)=x</annotation></semantics></math>. The empirical CDF is <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{n}(x)=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}\bm{1}(V_{t}\leq x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{n}(x)=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}\bm{1}(V_{t}\leq x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Classical statistics include the Kolmogorov–Smirnov and Anderson–Darling statistics:</p>
<table id="S6.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{x\in[0,1]}\left(F(x)-F_{n}(x)\right)^{2}\quad\text{and}\quad\int_{0}^{1}\left(\frac{F(x)-F_{n}(x)}{\sqrt{x(1-x)}}\right)^{2}\operatorname{d}\!x\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{x\in[0,1]}\left(F(x)-F_{n}(x)\right)^{2}\quad\text{and}\quad\int_{0}^{1}\left(\frac{F(x)-F_{n}(x)}{\sqrt{x(1-x)}}\right)^{2}\operatorname{d}\!x\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">These statistics cannot be written as sums of functionals of <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, the Kolmogorov–Smirnov statistic is not making
use of the fact that under the null hypothesis the variance of <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(x)-F_{n}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(x)-F_{n}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(1-x)/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(1-x)/n</annotation></semantics></math>.
This suggests a weighted Kolmogorov–Smirnov statistic:</p>
<table id="S6.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{x\in(0,1)}\frac{F(x)-F_{n}(x)}{\sqrt{x(1-x)}}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{x\in(0,1)}\frac{F(x)-F_{n}(x)}{\sqrt{x(1-x)}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which was introduced and analysed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Anderson and Darling (1952)</a></cite> as a goodness-of-fit test. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Donoho and Jin (2004)</a></cite> also studied this statistic in the context of multiple hypotheses
as we do here, but with a less complex structure for the alternative.
As it turns out, this statistic would yield about the same theory as our choice.
The statistic used here is based on the observation that <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(x)-F_{n}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(x)-F_{n}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is expected to be large for values of <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in[1/2,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in[1/2,1]</annotation></semantics></math>,
so the <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{x}</annotation></semantics></math> term in the denominator has little impact. Moreover, rather than taking a supremum we average ‘uniformly’ on buckets
<math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1/2],[1/2,3/4],[3/4,7/8],\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1/2],[1/2,3/4],[3/4,7/8],\ldots</annotation></semantics></math>, which corresponds to</p>
<table id="S6.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{1-\epsilon}\frac{F(x)-F_{n}(x)}{(1-x)^{3/2}}\operatorname{d}\!x=\frac{2}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}\min\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon}}\,,\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-V_{t}}}\right)-4+2\sqrt{\epsilon}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{1-\epsilon}\frac{F(x)-F_{n}(x)}{(1-x)^{3/2}}\operatorname{d}\!x=\frac{2}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}\min\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon}}\,,\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-V_{t}}}\right)-4+2\sqrt{\epsilon}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">which except for a scale and a shift is the proposed statistic.
The truncation is needed to ensure the statistic has well-controlled tails under the null hypothesis.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Weighted detectors</h3>

<div id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proposed detection mechanism is entirely independent of the model.
Detection can be improved enormously given access to a low-fidelity surrogate model.
Consider the situation in <a href="#Thmtheorem9" title="Example 9 (rare high entropy). ‣ Step 2: Case-by-case argument ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Example</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> where most tokens are nearly deterministic.
If the detector has access to a classifier <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:\Sigma^{*}\to\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:\Sigma^{*}\to\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(A_{1},\ldots,A_{t-1})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(A_{1},\ldots,A_{t-1})=0</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is close to a Dirac, then a better test statistic
is <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{n}\phi(A_{1},\ldots,A_{t-1})S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{n}\phi(A_{1},\ldots,A_{t-1})S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, which can then be compared to the critical
value for sample size <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{n}\phi(A_{1},\ldots,A_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{n}\phi(A_{1},\ldots,A_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assuming that <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is accurate, then this approach reduces the detection time for <a href="#Thmtheorem9" title="Example 9 (rare high entropy). ‣ Step 2: Case-by-case argument ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Example</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> from <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{O}(1/\beta^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{O}(1/\beta^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{O}(1/\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{O}(1/\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Alternatively, <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> can be real-valued (and even learned). Concretely, suppose that <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:\Sigma^{*}\to[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:\Sigma^{*}\to[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and detection has the form</p>
<table id="S6.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T=\bm{1}\left(\sum_{t=1}^{n}\phi(A_{1},\ldots,A_{t-1})S_{t}\geq\tau_{\star}\right)\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T=\bm{1}\left(\sum_{t=1}^{n}\phi(A_{1},\ldots,A_{t-1})S_{t}\geq\tau_{\star}\right)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}=S(V_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}=S(V_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as in <a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
Since <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}=\phi(A_{1},\ldots,A_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}=\phi(A_{1},\ldots,A_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> only depends on <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, under the null hypothesis <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> are independent. Hence, you can
still use Monte-Carlo to calculate a data-dependent critical threshold <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="S6.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\left(\sum_{t=1}^{n}\alpha_{t}S_{t}\geq\tau_{\star}\bigg|(\alpha_{t})_{t=1}^{n}\right)=\delta\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="2.100em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\left(\sum_{t=1}^{n}\alpha_{t}S_{t}\geq\tau_{\star}\bigg|(\alpha_{t})_{t=1}^{n}\right)=\delta\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Theoretically, by repeating the argument in <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ Step 2: Case-by-case argument ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, with <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>-probability at least <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S6.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{n}\alpha_{t}S_{t}=\tilde{O}\left(\sqrt{\sum_{t=1}^{n}\alpha_{t}^{2}}+\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon}}\right)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{n}\alpha_{t}S_{t}=\tilde{O}\left(\sqrt{\sum_{t=1}^{n}\alpha_{t}^{2}}+\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon}}\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Repeating also the proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma 6. ‣ Step 2: Case-by-case argument ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> shows that with <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-probability at least <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S6.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{n}\alpha_{t}S_{t}=\Omega\left(\sum_{t=1}^{n}\alpha_{t}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})\right)-\tilde{O}\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon}}+\sqrt{\sum_{t=1}^{n}\alpha_{t}^{2}}\right)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{n}\alpha_{t}S_{t}=\Omega\left(\sum_{t=1}^{n}\alpha_{t}G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})\right)-\tilde{O}\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon}}+\sqrt{\sum_{t=1}^{n}\alpha_{t}^{2}}\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.5" class="ltx_p">This is a complicated expression to optimise because <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\epsilon}(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\epsilon}(p)</annotation></semantics></math> depends on <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. A reasonable approximation in many practical scenarios is
<math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\epsilon}(p)\approx G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\epsilon}(p)\approx G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(p)</annotation></semantics></math> for some constant <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=1/10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=1/10</annotation></semantics></math>). Whenever this approximation is reasonable and <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}=G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}=G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, then detection occurs once</p>
<table id="S6.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{n}G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{t})^{2}=\tilde{\Omega}(1)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{n}G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{t})^{2}=\tilde{\Omega}(1)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Of course, this choice of <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> depends on <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> that is generally not known. An interesting question is how to choose <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> robustly when <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> can only
be estimated; and also in the case that <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})\approx G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\epsilon}(P_{t})\approx G^{\text{\scriptsize$\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}$}}(P_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is a poor approximation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Asymptotics of the critical statistic</h3>

<div id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Lindeberg–Feller central limit theorem provides an asymptotic approximation of <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in <a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.
When <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> has law <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}([0,1])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}([0,1])</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="S6.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[S(U)]=0\quad\text{and}\quad\mathbb{E}[S(U)^{2}]=\log(1/\varepsilon)-O(1)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[S(U)]=0\quad\text{and}\quad\mathbb{E}[S(U)^{2}]=\log(1/\varepsilon)-O(1)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Hence, with <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=\log(1/\delta)/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=\log(1/\delta)/n</annotation></semantics></math> the central limit theorem approximation of <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> for large <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S6.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tau_{\star}\sim\Phi^{-1}(1-\delta)\sqrt{n\log n}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tau_{\star}\sim\Phi^{-1}(1-\delta)\sqrt{n\log n}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is the cumulative distribution function of the standard Gaussian.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Non-optimality of subexponential statistics</h3>

<div id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A random variable <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is called <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-subexponential if <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\exp(|X/\sigma|)]\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\exp(|X/\sigma|)]\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vershynin, 2018</a>)</cite>.
Our choice of <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is a truncated power law under the null hypothesis, which is not subexponential for any <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=O(1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
On the other hand, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Aaronson (2022)</a></cite> chose <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to be exponentially distributed
and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dathathri et al. (2024)</a></cite> essentially chose the statistic to be Gaussian (more precisely, a convolution of Bernoulli’s).
Both of these choices are <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-subexponential with <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=\Theta(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=\Theta(1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Suppose that the statistics <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> are scaled and shifted so that under the null hypothesis <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{0}[S_{t}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{0}[S_{t}]=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{0}[S_{t}^{2}]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{0}[S_{t}^{2}]=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{0}[\exp(|S_{t}/\sigma|)]\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{0}[\exp(|S_{t}/\sigma|)]\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>
for some <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=O(1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
We argue under these conditions that using a detector of the form</p>
<table id="S6.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T=\bm{1}\left(\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}\geq\tau\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T=\bm{1}\left(\sum_{t=1}^{n}S_{t}\geq\tau\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">cannot lead to near-optimal detection.
To see why, under the alternative hypothesis, using <a href="#Thmtheorem21" title="Lemma 21. ‣ Appendix A Technical inequalities ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>,</p>
<table id="S6.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{1}[S_{t}|P_{t}]=\sum_{a\in\Sigma}\mathbb{E}_{1}[S_{t}\bm{1}(A_{t}=a)|P_{t}]\leq\frac{5}{2}\sigma\sum_{a\in\Sigma}h(P_{t}(a))\leq 5\sigma H(P_{t})\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{1}[S_{t}|P_{t}]=\sum_{a\in\Sigma}\mathbb{E}_{1}[S_{t}\bm{1}(A_{t}=a)|P_{t}]\leq\frac{5}{2}\sigma\sum_{a\in\Sigma}h(P_{t}(a))\leq 5\sigma H(P_{t})\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(p)=-p\log(p)-(1-p)\log(1-p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(p)=-p\log(p)-(1-p)\log(1-p)</annotation></semantics></math> is the binary entropy.
Since we assumed that <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{0}[S_{t}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{0}[S_{t}]=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{0}[S_{t}^{2}]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{0}[S_{t}^{2}]=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the central limit theorem suggests the critical threshold satisfies <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\star}=\tilde{\Theta}(\sqrt{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\star}=\tilde{\Theta}(\sqrt{n})</annotation></semantics></math>,
it follows that detection occurs only when <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\sum_{t=1}^{n}H(P_{t})=\tilde{\Omega}(\sqrt{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\sum_{t=1}^{n}H(P_{t})=\tilde{\Omega}(\sqrt{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, which when <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=O(1)</annotation></semantics></math> implies that <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=\tilde{\Omega}(1/\bar{H}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=\tilde{\Omega}(1/\bar{H}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
We showed in <a href="#Thmtheorem8" title="Example 8 (constant low entropy). ‣ Step 2: Case-by-case argument ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Example</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, however, that the power law statistic yields detection once
<math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=\tilde{\Omega}(1/\bar{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=\tilde{\Omega}(1/\bar{H})</annotation></semantics></math>.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tsur et al. (2025b)</a></cite> also noted the importance of using a heavier-tailed statistic for more efficient detection.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Logarithmic factors</h3>

<div id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There is a logarithmic factor gap between the upper and lower bounds.
The upper bound is probably not improvable for the proposed power law detection scheme.
In certain cases (see <a href="#Thmtheorem9" title="Example 9 (rare high entropy). ‣ Step 2: Case-by-case argument ‣ 3 Power law detection ‣ Refined Detection for Gumbel Watermarking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Example</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) the bound on the detection time
for the newly proposed detection scheme is worse than the bound provided by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Aaronson (2022)</a></cite>.
Since the watermarking scheme is the same for both, one can of course combine the tests proposed here
with that suggested by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Aaronson (2022)</a></cite> at the cost of a union bound.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px8" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Acknowledgements</h3>

<div id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Many thanks to Marcus Hutter and András György for useful discussion and suggestions.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
